  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hi. Well, to be completely honest, it’s a bit of a long story, but I suppose the main thing that brings me in today is this... this constant restless feeling I’ve been dealing with. It’s just always there in the background. It feels exactly like I’m wound way too tight, like a toy that's been cranked up too much, and I just can’t fully settle. \n\nAnd I mean, I really try to. I work as a wholesale buyer, so my days are usually full of these incredibly long, drawn-out seasonal planning meetings where you just have to sit there and look attentive while someone goes over vendor contracts or supply chain logistics. And I just can't settle into my chair. I'm constantly shifting or feeling this urge to move. \n\nBut it’s not even just at work where it’s a problem, which is why I finally decided to make an appointment. I try to do things on my own time that are supposed to be relaxing, you know? Like, I took up painting recently to try and give myself a creative outlet, and I’ve been going to this yoga class on Thursday evenings because everyone says it's so good for finding your center and unwinding. But even then, when I’m supposed to be calmly sitting there, whether I'm painting a canvas or just doing yoga and trying to breathe, I just have this tight, restless energy. I can't just relax and let go. It’s like my body completely refuses to just sit still and be calm, and it’s just getting so frustrating trying to manage it all the time when I just want to enjoy a quiet moment.",
